# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example
# Copy this file to .env for local development: cp .env.example .env
# This file lists VARIABLE NAMES ONLY. Never commit real secret values.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public canonical site URL (used for canonical tags, sitemap, JSON-LD).
# Safe to expose in the frontend build.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://example-montaj-mobila.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The site ships by default using Netlify Forms, which requires NO
# secrets in the frontend or in environment variables at all — Netlify
# handles submission storage and email notification from its dashboard
# (Site configuration > Forms > Form notifications).
#
# The variables below are ONLY needed if you choose to enable the
# OPTIONAL Netlify Function described in README.md / SECURITY.md for
# transactional email via a provider such as Resend, Postmark or
# SendGrid. They must be set in the Netlify dashboard under
# Site configuration > Environment variables — NEVER in this repo,
# NEVER in frontend code, and NEVER committed to git.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Transactional email provider API key (server-side function only).
# EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Verified "from" address for transactional email (server-side function only).
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# Destination address that should receive quote-request notifications.
# EMAIL_TO_ADDRESS=

# Comma-separated list of allowed origins for the function's CORS check.
# Should be your exact production domain, e.g. https://example-montaj-mobila.md
# FUNCTION_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=
